Therefore, this type of test is best suited to end-to-end (integration) tests, which would involve setting up the scenario, making calls to the API, and then asserting on the post conditions. Unit tests, specifically PUT tests, are typically built on the assumption that the system under test performs its job without interacting with other components (e.g., database, external services). 

